# title: Exporter {job} on {instance} is scraped fine but cannot read its source
# severity: error
# component: monitoring
# key: job,instance
# note: the scrape target itself is health=up, so an `up == 0` alert never fires. The exporter's OWN gauge says it cannot reach what it exports (wrong grant, password, DSN), so every metric it should produce is missing — this is how a broken postgres_exporter goes unnoticed for months.
({__name__=~".+_exporter_last_scrape_error"} == 1) or ({__name__=~"(pg|mysql|redis|mongodb|elasticsearch|rabbitmq|memcached|pgbouncer|kafka|haproxy|nginx|apache)_up"} == 0)
